{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/82799-looking-for-players-for-scion","id":82799,"title":"Looking for players for Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-02T15:12:33-08:00","id":82799,"title":"Looking for players for Scion","content":"I wanted to join a play by post Scion game but when I looked for it, there wasn't any started. I was wondering if anyone was interested to start one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: I'll be the Storyteller.<br /> - 3 players max (4, if need be).<br /> - The game would be 80% social/mental and 20% physical.<br /> - The game will be settled in New York.<br /> <br /> House rules: (none other than the character creation process has been talked about)<br /> - No pantheon restricted but fanmade ones.<br /> - No God restricted (if added by fans, I would like to read the God description first)<br /> - No age restricted (I tend to make my players create young adults but I'll try something different <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> - No calling restricted<br /> - There's no need to prioritize the Attribute categories. You have 18 points. You are free to add them wherever you want as long as the attribute tops out at 5 dots.<br /> - Abilities: I use the favored abilities rules. For the specialties, the more specific the term used, the better. Instead of &quot;art (music)&quot;, you may write &quot;art (classical music)&quot;. It sounds boring I guess but it would be easier (for me) to create plots.<br /> - Same rules for Birthrights. If specific powers, you would need my approval first.<br /> - Same rules for Knacks and Boons. For Lightning Sprinter, if you'd rather swim or fly faster, you are allowed to.<br /> - Same rules for Virtues. You may switch one single Virtue that might not fit with your concept.<br /> - Legend: you may start with 2 or 3.<br /> - Same amount of bonus points. Same costs.<br /> <br /> Legend can't be bought. I'll grant it when the time comes.<br /> <br /> <br /> When the game starts, every player must post before posting again. For example, player A posted a description of what his character is about to do to break in jail. Player A will have to wait for player B, C and D to play before posting anything more. No limit of words per post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","user":"Wickedgrail","date":". 04-04-2014, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T18:58:11-08:00","id":82890,"title":"","content":"I would be interested! I recently got ahold of this game, and I've been really interested in playing!<br /> <br /> Any details on settings/storylines?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, what pantheons would be allowed? Or are you hoping for someone else to ST?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","user":"Murder-chan","date":". 03-02-2014, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T23:17:48-08:00","id":82993,"title":"","content":"I've never STed before in a play by post game so I don't know how to handle one. I'd be okay to ST, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T23:33:36-08:00","id":83007,"title":"","content":"I'm absolutely interested in playing. I'm currently preparing to run a Werewolf: the Apocalypse PbP game (just finishing my setting notes before I start a recruitment post), so I would not be comfortable trying to ST two games at once, but I am absolutely up for playing. What kind of game did you have in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T02:24:03-08:00","id":83053,"title":"","content":"Most of plots that I've written included a lot of battles which I find entertaining around a table, with friends screaming and miming what they think their characters would do. In a play by post game, I would like something more social. I would not remove any battles but less for sure. It might looks like the Avengers. Something like SHIELD looking for Scions or Titanspawns or whatever creatures that might be supernatural. I would not want to restrict my players not to use their powers so that they will not get caught. What I like about Scion is Boons and Knacks because without &quot;magic&quot; it will look like WoD and I'm certainly not playing Scion to play powerless Scion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My games tend to use same Knacks and Boons. Fertility, Justice, Guardian and so on are unpopular in my games. I would love to see those... bloom <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> As far as pantheons are concerned, I have no restrictions but the fanmade ones. I like to be familiar with things and unfortunately I'm not interested in those pantheons enough to let my players use them.<br /> <br /> To sum it up:<br /> - more social/ mental, less battles (still be able to kick some butts, of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) <br /> - Struggles between using freely your powers or more discreetly but no restriction to using powers intended.<br /> - Uncommon Boons and Knacks (such as Math genius, Teaching prodigy) are mostly welcome.<br /> - No fanmade pantheons. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T03:25:09-08:00","id":83068,"title":"","content":"A government organization trying to track down Scions? MIght be interesting, as long as it doesn't start to feel too much like we're a bunch of costumed superheroes. Anything else to keep in mind while coming up with concepts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T03:40:33-08:00","id":83072,"title":"","content":"umm, I'm not sure whether I want to involve the government. The organization might not be mortal at all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can't think of anything else... any questions maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T03:54:52-08:00","id":83073,"title":"","content":"Hmm. That does sound better; I just assumed government when you made the comparison to SHIELD. I'm thinking of some criminal type backgrounds, actually. Your mention of having to use powers discreetly popped it into my head. Something like the leader of a street gang, or a member of the Mafia or the Yakuza perhaps, who uses his divine powers for his own gain while also protecting the world from titanspawn and such. Is that a concept that would work for what you have in mind, or would you prefer something a little less... morally ambiguous? As for questions, I would ask how many players you're looking for, and whether you're planning to use any house rules we should know about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T05:17:34-08:00","id":83098,"title":"","content":"I like characters who struggle to be what they need to be and who they really want to be. The more ambiguous the better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> so a leader of a gang is okay. Even immoral is okay for me but<br /> when creating your character, I like &quot;extreme&quot; characters. Only one dot in an Attribute is perfectly okay, even better actually. It's easier to see an evolution.<br /> For Scion 2e, they would allow players to handle theirs fatebindings. So, don't hesitate to create friends, enemies, families, exes and so on.<br /> <br /> How many players: I want to start with 3 max (4 if need be). The clearer the game, the better.<br /> <br /> House rules: if you're talking about the character creation process:<br /> - No pantheon restricted but fanmade ones.<br /> - No God restricted (if added by fans, I would like to read the God description first)<br /> - No age restricted (I tend to make my players create young adults but I'll try something different <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> - No calling restricted<br /> - There's no need to prioritize the Attribute categories. You have 18 points. You are free to add them wherever you want as long as the attribute tops out at 5 dots.<br /> - Abilities: I use the favored abilities rules. For the specialties, the more specific the term used, the better. Instead of &quot;art (music)&quot;, you may write &quot;art (classical music)&quot;. It sounds boring I guess but it would be easier (for me) to create plots.<br /> - Same rules for Birthrights. If specific powers, you would need my approval first.<br /> - Same rules for Knacks and Boons. For Lightning Sprinter, if you'd rather swim or fly faster, you are allowed to.<br /> - Same rules for Virtues. You may switch one single Virtue that might not be fit with your concept.<br /> - Legend: you may start with 2 or 3.<br /> - Same amount of bonus points. Same costs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Any more questions? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T06:05:07-08:00","id":83126,"title":"","content":"Hm. Are you planning to have the characters, for the Heroic portion of their adventures at least, tied to a specific city or location as a sort of &quot;home base,&quot; or are you planning to have a more world-spanning chronicle? If the latter, do you have an objection to characters who have such roots? After all, if my character is a gang leader or a crime boss, it's impractical to bring the whole gang/mafia family/whatever with him on adventures, LOL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T08:04:51-08:00","id":83171,"title":"","content":"I tried too hard to move my players to different locations for unknown reasons and I don't think it helped creating any relationship. It might sound too original but I think North America is a safe bet... hehehe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (the original part was ironic). I haven't decided yet where it would be but it will be a specific city (probably New York). I would want my players to travel sometimes... you could save a Relic to invoke your family. If you don't want them to know about your divine blond, create a Relic that would make them forget and not suprised to be invoked... Choose Aesir, it'd be easier heheh<br /> <br /> Edit: if there were things you disagree with, do no hesitate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T08:53:01-08:00","id":83215,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm actually leaning in the direction of the Azlanti. Probably Tezcatlipoca. I had thought about LA, but New York (or any other major city) should work just fine. Your chronicle, obviously. :-) Anyway, I'm definitely thinking that the gang knows about my character's divine nature; I envision them as both a gang and a cult. The normal criminal activity and turf wars, but with the added fun of sacrificing their victims to the gods of the Azlanti (and, eventually, to my character as well). However, I don't like the idea of summoning them around with a relic; when my character is out of town, they stay home and defend the turf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T10:58:31-08:00","id":83309,"title":"","content":"Oh, I like the sound of it so far~ Also, I really like mafia, so Nutiket's character is sounding intriguing.<br /> <br /> If we're allowed to use the Companion pantheons, then I'm kind of inclined to make a Scion of Shiva, but I'm a little iffy just because there are issues with how 1e portrayed him &gt;w&gt;;; If I made a Scion of Shiva, I'd prefer to use this version: <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/shiva.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/shiva.htm</a><br /> <br /> But I'm not entirely sure I want to make a Scion of Shiva right now anyway. I kind of have an idea for a daughter of Hades who as creepypasta followers, which might be a little morally ambiguous, but hey. Morally ambiguous sounds like a reasonable thing, right? Good for stories?<br /> <br /> And I'm glad the game will be focused on Mental/Social things, as well, so I'm thinking she might be the kind of person who's very well versed in morbid things. But she's also the kind of person to brutally abuse her powers as a Scion. . .. Hmm :|a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T11:31:02-08:00","id":83322,"title":"","content":"The more I think about it, the more I'm leaning in the direction of a street gang rather than the mafia. This way, I can build it from the ground up and not have a whole entrenched power structure to deal with. Hope that's OK. So, what exactly do you mean by &quot;creepypasta followers&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T11:46:59-08:00","id":83331,"title":"","content":"Street gang would definitely be less complicated. Would you be planning on having them grow over the course of the story?<br /> <br /> Well, people go about writing creepypasta and reading creepypasta, and that could, theoretically, generate Legend, right? Since Legend comes from being known, and there are all sorts of gods who try to mimic legends and stories in order to latch onto the power, so I guess I'm thinking of a 2-5 ghosts who are mimicking creepypasta stories to become more powerful.<br /> <br /> So they might have to do unsavory things for that power, given their origins in horror stories. I'm not a huge fan of creepypasta, but this idea hasn't wanted to leave me alone. Especially with a shadier, more immoral Scion who is totally willing to let them do this for her own gain, and might even spend her off time documenting their activities to encourage it, thought that might be going a bit further.<br /> <br /> So really, in the beginning she'd just have ghost followers, and then they'd get creepier as time goes on, and start becoming more powerful and creepier over time. She probably won't fit in with her pantheon too well, though.<br /> <br /> I guess this begs the question, though, whether I should be using &quot;guide&quot; or &quot;follower&quot;, since they wouldn't be latching onto the same story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T13:51:56-08:00","id":83439,"title":"","content":"I was about to read Shiva's &quot;new&quot; description but it seems like you chose Hades instead. Followers sounds closer to your description. Guides... guide Scions. I don't see those ghosts as guides... Moreover, there would be too many guides, you wouldn't know who to listen to...<br /> <br /> Everything is okay with me so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T18:37:05-08:00","id":83661,"title":"","content":"Ahah, sorry about that. I will always be partial to playing a Scion of Shiva, but I have less of an idea for that character, so I'm gonna run with a scion of Hades right now. And psssh. Clearly you listen to whichever guide is advising you to do what you actually wanna do, right?<br /> <br /> Excellent -- I'll start making a character sheet sometime in the next day or two ahaha Once I get some other things figured out~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T22:38:25-08:00","id":83785,"title":"","content":"Well, I certainly do want the gang to grow over time, but that begs a question. Grail, do I need to buy the entire gang with dots of followers? Or just some of them? Or just the important ones? Or none at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T23:16:04-08:00","id":83801,"title":"","content":"Murder: if you don't mind taking some time to think about a Scion of Shiva, I won't mind at all.<br /> <br /> Nutiket: You'd have to spend dots if you use them in battles. Otherwise, you'll be wasting them. Instead, you could spend dots in Guide. Then one of them will be your right hand and helping you looking for the place to be and telling you everything that you might miss... a traitor or worse... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> 2 dots if you want him or her to be mortal. 3, if you want him or her to be supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T23:30:48-08:00","id":83806,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I understand what you mean by &quot;wasting them.&quot; Do you mean that buying them as followers would be wasting them, or that not buying them as followers would be wasting them? --- Edit: I do very much like the idea of purchasing a Guide to act as my characters right hand man or woman. A 3-dot guide usually means a Scion; is that what you had in mind when you referred to a possible supernatural guide, or were you thinking of something else? As for the rest of the gang, I have no intention of using them in scion-level combat or bringing them on adventures, generally speaking. They would be involved in combat if the gang itself was attacked, though, or if the gang attacked some other gang or some such like that. I imagine this would mostly be in downtime unless you chose to incorporate it into the overall storyline. So, with that in mind, what do you suggest in terms of whether or not I should purchase gang members as followers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":".  Clarification after further thought 03-04-2014, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T05:11:10-08:00","id":83905,"title":"","content":"You would waste your dots if you buy them as followers and not use them in battles. 3-dot guide can be any supernatural being with no more than Legend 2. Can be a ghost, Could be any supernatural being but not higher than Legend 2. If your intention is to make him to help you with his knowledge (Culture and Occult would be at least 2), 2-dot guide is enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T06:09:26-08:00","id":83915,"title":"","content":"So, if I didn't buy them as followers, I should just describe the more important gang members as part of my character history? Perhaps as fatebound mortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T09:25:11-08:00","id":84006,"title":"","content":"That's right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Fatebound them is good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:59:18-08:00","id":84065,"title":"","content":"As for the guide... how would you feel about a Nagual? In mesoamerican mythology, a Nagual is a human (usually a sorcerer of some kind) who had the power to change into an animal. In this case, a Jaguar. No Epic Attributes or such. Does that sound like it might be acceptable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T15:04:29-08:00","id":84233,"title":"","content":"I guess that you stick to Tezcatlipoca then? Nagual works for me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Naguals are protectors. Make sure you choose the animal that fits your background. Or, if you're willing to spend 4-dot, the Nagual can be a shape-shifter (limited to animals). He can be any animals or a mortal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T18:14:20-08:00","id":84312,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that a Nagual was a human that changed into an animal. You seem to be implying that it is the other way around; perhaps we are looking at different sources? And, anyway, can I convince you to let him/her be a 3-dot guide since the shapechanging would be his only power? I mean, in the grand scheme of Scion, is a guide who can change from a mundane human to a mundane animal really worth 4 dots of birthrights?<br /> <br /> Edit: And yes, I'm feeling pretty settled on Tezcatlipoca.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T20:09:31-08:00","id":84346,"title":"","content":"Hmm. . . . I've been thinking of what I'd want to for a Scion of Shiva, and I'm kind of pondering either a destructive street-kid type who's had some sort of recent rags-to-riches story and is struggling to fit in with higher society and leave their violent, delinquent past behind them, of a war-god type figure.<br /> <br /> Kind of like that really strong fighter who isn't associated with a particular gang but who most gangs are pretty terrified of anyway (I've probably been watching too much anime). . . but she recently tried to settle down with a rich millionaire type figure for ~true love~ and then her estranged father showed up at her wedding . . . and that got the tabloid's attention.<br /> <br /> Actually, someone like that could be fun to play. She'd probably start as a predominantly physical/mental character, but then grow mostly towards a more social/mental character. Hmm. . . :|a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T21:08:12-08:00","id":84365,"title":"","content":"How old were you thinking, Murder-chan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T21:45:16-08:00","id":84383,"title":"","content":"Hm, I was going to offer up a Pesedjet Scion of Khonsu who goes out at night fighting crime while living on welfare...but you all seem to have deep ties to the criminal underworld, so that might not work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T21:55:57-08:00","id":84388,"title":"","content":"You could fight OTHER criminals. There are plenty out there. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T23:19:22-08:00","id":84425,"title":"","content":"I'll be leaving soon so I'll just reply to Darksol: if you all fit in the &quot;same world&quot;, everything would make more sense. Social in the criminal world is funnier. You can talk.... not enough to convince you? Kill him! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh and Nutiket: For me, a Nagual is a mortal that can shapeshift into an animal... go for 3-dot guide <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Murder: A female character in the Band will be very good. Love female characters. Especially strong ones. Can't wait to read her background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","user":"Wickedgrail","date":". 03-05-2014, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T06:24:48-08:00","id":84532,"title":"","content":"I don't know, Grail. There's a lot of potential for drama there. A vigilante, living on food stamps, fighting criminals, forced to work with people he despises, people who live the high life (relatively speaking) by preying on the people of the city he protects. He's forced to work with us for the greater good, and can't take us down like he wants to. Will he eventually convince us to mend our evil ways? Or will we draw him to the dark side? Or will we find some uneasy truce, each of us ignoring the parts of the others' lives we find distasteful? Maybe we'll even settle our differences another way, with the criminals toning down their more blatant excesses and even helping the vigilante find the scum that are worse than they are? You're the ST, of course, but I hope you'll give it some thought; there's potential for some rich, if challenging, RP here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T06:43:55-08:00","id":84543,"title":"","content":"Looks like your Nagual is more than a mere guide. Every suggestion sounds good. No players of mine use Guides because they aren't worth it around my table... if you're willing to give him some depths, I'll be glad to see how far this Nagual could go. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","user":"Wickedgrail","date":". 03-05-2014, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T10:24:02-08:00","id":84693,"title":"","content":"I also think Darksol's idea for a Scion on welfare fighting crime would be a great roleplay possibility~ They don't have to get along, they just have to not kill each other. And I know my scion is definitely trying to leave her delinquent ways behind her, so a less criminal member of the band might definitely help balance out the influence of Nutiket's character.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T13:34:28-08:00","id":84810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/82799-looking-for-players-for-scion?p=84532#post84532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, Grail. There's a lot of potential for drama there. A vigilante, living on food stamps, fighting criminals, forced to work with people he despises, people who live the high life (relatively speaking) by preying on the people of the city he protects. He's forced to work with us for the greater good, and can't take us down like he wants to. Will he eventually convince us to mend our evil ways? Or will we draw him to the dark side? Or will we find some uneasy truce, each of us ignoring the parts of the others' lives we find distasteful? Maybe we'll even settle our differences another way, with the criminals toning down their more blatant excesses and even helping the vigilante find the scum that are worse than they are? You're the ST, of course, but I hope you'll give it some thought; there's potential for some rich, if challenging, RP here.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/82799-looking-for-players-for-scion?p=84543#post84543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like your Nagual is more than a mere guide. Every suggestion sounds good. No players of mine use Guides because they aren't worth it around my table... if you're willing to give him some depths, I'll be glad to see how far this Nagual could go. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Grail, my message above was about Darksol's proposed Scion, not about my character's Nagual guide. Sorry for the confusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/82799-looking-for-players-for-scion?p=84693#post84693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think Darksol's idea for a Scion on welfare fighting crime would be a great roleplay possibility~ They don't have to get along, they just have to not kill each other. And I know my scion is definitely trying to leave her delinquent ways behind her, so a less criminal member of the band might definitely help balance out the influence of Nutiket's character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, did you just call my character a bad influence? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":". 03-05-2014, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T14:52:24-08:00","id":84861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/82799-looking-for-players-for-scion?p=84693#post84693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think Darksol's idea for a Scion on welfare fighting crime would be a great roleplay possibility~ They don't have to get along, they just have to not kill each other. And I know my scion is definitely trying to leave her delinquent ways behind her, so a less criminal member of the band might definitely help balance out the influence of Nutiket's character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go for that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Nutiket: Oh, my bad...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T14:54:44-08:00","id":84864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/82799-looking-for-players-for-scion?p=84810#post84810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, did you just call my character a bad influence? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if the shoe fits <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T17:17:52-08:00","id":84938,"title":"","content":"Hope no one has written the background yet because everything may happen in Connecticut. New York is a too simple choice and since other cities are part of the most dangerous ones (and out of 25, 3 of them are in Connecticut), I'd probably choose this State to settle my game. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T18:09:02-08:00","id":84968,"title":"","content":"Sounds good to me! I don't know much about any big cities right now anyway, ahah ^-^;;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T18:43:28-08:00","id":84984,"title":"","content":"That's fine, I guess. Which city are you using, so I can get started on my research? You are aware of how small the cities in Connecticut are, though, right? I think Bridgeport is the largest at about 150,000 people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T21:58:24-08:00","id":85101,"title":"","content":"Connecticut eh? Never been there, but this is what we have googlemaps for.<br /> <br /> While I agree that having a Lo-budget vigilante working alonside you all would be hilarious, I'm worried about the rough start that's likely to generate. Can you just imagine meeting this guy after he's thrashed the majority of your still-mortal gang for human trafficking or whatnot? Hell my pantheon is gonna HATE me, I'll have to trade out Order or I'll have virtue extremities just TALKING to you all...<br /> <br /> Of course, my other idea would take us into fanmade pantheon territory over at JSR: An Annuna scion of Ereshkigal who is a Professional Assassin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T03:33:11-08:00","id":85213,"title":"","content":"I read how many people they are but I didn't realize until now... it might be a little small...<br /> I was looking for dangerous cities... but I guess New York will have to do... I wanted a different city but seems like the biggest one was the easiest choice...sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T06:59:44-08:00","id":85278,"title":"","content":"No need to apologize. I'm sure Bridgeport can work if that's what you want to do; I just wanted to make sure you were aware of its size. It's your chronicle, though. Your choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T07:04:20-08:00","id":85280,"title":"","content":"I wanted a less known city but still famous for its danger... The Bronx is dangerous but too common... I was actually ready to start at Camden, New Jersey.<br /> <br /> Well, let's vote between New York and Camben. Since we're four and both cities suit me, I let you guys decide <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","user":"Wickedgrail","date":"I wrote Camben... I was probably thinking about Campbell...) 03-06-2014, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T07:36:22-08:00","id":85307,"title":"","content":"LOL, it's &quot;Camden,&quot; not &quot;Camben.&quot; I actually live just east of Camden. For those unaware, Camden is a small city in South Jersey, right across the river from Philadelphia. It consistently ranks with the highest per capita rates of violent crime in the United.States, though this is sometimes overlooked because larger cities have more murders and appear at a glance to be more dangerous. For reference, Camden's murder rate is 60.6 per 100,000 citizens. That is 12 times the national average; the overall crime rate is 5 times the national average. Camden is a hole. As interesting as Camden is, though, I would vote for New York. It's more cosmopolitan, much more diverse, and more interesting overall. Camden is just a slum. New York has slums, and also other stuff. The only thing Camden has to recommend it, besides overall blight, is being right across the river from Philly, but it seems like a bad idea to have to go to another city every time we want to see something other than urban decay. So, between those two options, I vote for New York City.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T08:06:29-08:00","id":85335,"title":"","content":"Camden... how could I spell it wrong? My bad...<br /> <br /> I just edited my first post so that everything we've agreed with are written there.<br /> <br /> Besides the city, there are lots of houserules for Epic attributes and Purviews. We won't throw any dice so it's up to you to tell something that is possible for your Scion to do. If any houserule is crucial for you, let me know and we'll talk about it (I'm thinking about Epic Dexterity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T08:25:10-08:00","id":85351,"title":"","content":"I am okay with whatever setting we get, so I'm going to just focus on Darksol's concerns, Re: low budget crime fighter alongside 1) gang leader and 1) former delinquent . . . .<br /> <br /> My Scion is still running away from the things she's done in her past, but while a major part of her character development is (hopefully) going to force her to come to terms with the fact that, yes, she used to be a very angry child who beat up other children, and then grew into a very angry adult who beat up other adults, and she's still angry no matter how much she tries to hide from it, she's still going to actively be trying to overcome the anger and become more of a team player and do good things, etc. But in the start, she's still going to be trying to maintain the illusion that she's just a well-to-do-young-bride. So while she's definitely hiding anything, there's no reason for their to be any tension between her and someone fighting crime. She won't be doing anything that would force someone else to make an Order role (especially in the beginning, when your pool for virtues will be lower, even with higher virtues), and by the time things with her past start catching up to her (<i>if</i> they actually do), it should be clear that she's changed a lot.<br /> <br /> And as for Nutiket's Scion, I'm not sure how obvious he wants his gang to be, but there's not necessarily any reason for his gang to be in anything particularly serious (well, okay, other than human sacrifices, and you definitely want to keep that on the down low and not tell your new buddies about it) or large scale, like human trafficking. They're not a mafia family (yet), so there's no real reason to start with conflict, unless you want to introduce that kind of rivalry from the beginning.<br /> <br /> And just because you have Order as a virtue doesn't mean you have to focus on it in the beginning -- but that's getting into what you want to do with your character, so I'll wander off to class now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T09:13:45-08:00","id":85386,"title":"","content":"I've actually decided to replace Order with Courage in order to facilitate a more...flexible morality. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The very act of vigilantism is already against the law, it would be hypocritical for me to do all this under the auspices of Order (especially since I'll probably be pulling some quasi-legal stunts to get results). The character will focus on Conviction and Harmony more than anything else seeing as how he's more of an avenging type of vigilante. The pantheon may not like it, but I'm looking to be a scion of Khonsu, and he technically predates the Pesedjet in their current format.<br /> (For his writeup I'm using Telgar's compilation of extra gods pdf over in the Scion forums)<br /> <br /> I'm alright with Camden or wherever, but if you want a large-scale brokedown city you could try Detroit. It's usually in the top 10 as far as illicit madness, you got the lake if you want water monsters, and the place is so broke that it's got lots of urban ruins for monsters to hide in.<br /> <br /> How exactly do we submit characters for approval? Do we PM them somehow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T15:51:33-08:00","id":85686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/82799-looking-for-players-for-scion?p=85101#post85101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Connecticut eh? Never been there, but this is what we have googlemaps for.<br /> <br /> While I agree that having a Lo-budget vigilante working alonside you all would be hilarious, I'm worried about the rough start that's likely to generate. Can you just imagine meeting this guy after he's thrashed the majority of your still-mortal gang for human trafficking or whatnot? Hell my pantheon is gonna HATE me, I'll have to trade out Order or I'll have virtue extremities just TALKING to you all...<br /> <br /> Of course, my other idea would take us into fanmade pantheon territory over at JSR: An Annuna scion of Ereshkigal who is a Professional Assassin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understand... You're talking about your Scion or Nutiket's? The final impression of your Scion is someone who rights wrongs at no cost. Edit: I think I understood. That might create some tension, which creates RP: the ST likes it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> More seriously, depending on how much you think your Occult would be, your Scion might be more understanding regarding to Aztec ceremonies. Crualties are part of the world and it's all the more true in the Overworld as your Scion should know for how he's treated by his own kind. Free for you to adjust your level of understanding. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Khonsu has been validated if you still want to choose this God to be yours.<br /> <br /> As far as character approval, I will need to take a look at them. PM it to me if you don't want the others to see your sheet.<br /> <br /> As for Detroit, I've thought about it but I wanted other cities... Anyway, let's keep it to New York city and that would be my final word <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Murder: Still okay with her background. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","user":"Wickedgrail","date":". 03-06-2014, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T19:47:48-08:00","id":85793,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming we're already post-visitation? I'm sending you the stats for the character now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T23:49:53-08:00","id":85861,"title":"","content":"You assume right <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T23:55:31-08:00","id":85866,"title":"","content":"I am at work right now, but I plan to get my sheet up in the morning when I get home. Darksol brings up an interesting point about virtues. The default Azlanti virtues are Conviction, Courage, Duty and Loyalty. I plan to focus on Conviction, and to a lesser extent on Loyalty. Duty, however, is somewhat antithetical to my character's focus. If I were smart, I'd replace it with something more condusive like Endurance or Vengeance. However, I prefer not to change a Scion's virtues from those of the Pantheon. I see virtues in Scion as a supernatural thing, a part of their Legend and divine nature. After all, if they were not, very Tom, Dick and Mortal would have them (as in, say, Exalted 2E, where nearly every sapient being has the virtues Compassion, Conviction, Temperance and Valor). I view the virtues as part and parcel of being in a particular pantheon; so, I do not change them, even when it would cause me inconvenience. My character is a violent criminal, and he makes no apology for that fact. However, he is also a Scion of the Azlanti, and so feels some small shred of Duty telling him what he is doing is, at least to some extent, wrong. This single dot of Duty can also be a seed. If, during the course of the chronicle (perhaps through the influence of the other PCs), my character does start to feel a stronger sense of duty, that seed might grow. I prefer to leave that potential intact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T09:58:09-08:00","id":86084,"title":"","content":"That all makes sense, so I suppose I don't need to change Order to Courage. But given the way the character operates I'll probably never gain more than the 1 dot in Order that I have since he finds too much issue with how rigid and shortsighted the law actually is. I don't need Courage to go into battle since you can do that with Conviction, and having a non-standard virtue means your PSP costs more anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T10:15:06-08:00","id":86100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/82799-looking-for-players-for-scion?p=86084#post86084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That all makes sense, so I suppose I don't need to change Order to Courage. But given the way the character operates I'll probably never gain more than the 1 dot in Order that I have since he finds too much issue with how rigid and shortsighted the law actually is. I don't need Courage to go into battle since you can do that with Conviction, and having a non-standard virtue means your PSP costs more anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, please don't misunderstand me. I was not suggesting that your character keep Order, or that you change your plans. I was simply explaining my decision to keep Duty, because otherwise it would look very odd. Also, depending on how things progress, and whether my character works to change his ways at all, I can see him increasing his Duty. Well, probably not higher than 2, but still an increase, if he changes that aspect of his personality over time. Anyway, I wasn't trying to influence you one way or the other on the issue; just explaining my decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T14:25:37-08:00","id":86264,"title":"","content":"nah it's alright. Even if you cancel out the first two reasons to switch back, the fact of having my PSP cost more still weighs in on staying with the classic virtues. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T02:41:49-08:00","id":86621,"title":"","content":"I intend to apply some rules for the game. Let me know how you feel about them.<br /> First, no limit of posting.<br /> Second, one should wait for every member to play before playing again (I would count as one, so, we're four). I want everyone to get the chance to act to proceed any further.<br /> Third, if two or more characters are involved in the same scene, here's two options: one could play every PC. That implies sharing your character sheets and backgrounds. The second option is to write what your character will do and wait for the other players to reply.<br /> I can't think of any other option right now so... let me know if there is more interesting one. I know that revealing his sheet is not that fun for some people.<br /> <br /> That's all for the rules, for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T05:08:15-08:00","id":86685,"title":"","content":"I am absolutely opposed to the idea of letting anyone else play my character. That does not work for me at all. By the same token, I have no interest in playing anyone else's character. I don't care much about sharing my sheet, but if someone else is playing my character, he's not my character (unless he's being mind controlled or something). Also, I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;no limit of posting,&quot; and how that relates to rule #2, that we have to wait for everyone to post before we can post again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T11:39:36-08:00","id":86899,"title":"","content":"I agree -- I would prefer not to share my character for other people to play ^-^;;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T12:29:54-08:00","id":86933,"title":"","content":"Let me clarify. You may not post again until every player posted. Some ST might allow you, let's say, 3 posts per day. There's no such rule. You can post as long as all players have played after you. That way, everyone takes part of the game. Is it clearer and do you agree with that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T13:35:49-08:00","id":86978,"title":"","content":"Ah, yes, that makes sense, though I hope you will be flexible if situations warrant, for example if 2 PCs are having a conversation while one is asleep or unconscious or otherwise occupied and not participating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T13:53:07-08:00","id":86984,"title":"","content":"Exceptional circumstances allow players to go against this rule. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T14:00:55-08:00","id":86990,"title":"","content":"Cool; I figured, I just wanted to be sure. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T14:28:30-08:00","id":87007,"title":"","content":"About XP. I will reward much more than suggested in the book. I tried different methods to make my players spend their XP but it was once too restricted (they could only spend points depending on what happened) or too conventional (very little XP). I even offered lots of XP but it didn't help them what was best to buy... (first-time players probably). <br /> I'll be trying a new system which would look like the video game one. You won't have to wait until the end of the chapter/storyline before earning XP. Every time something is worth to be getting <i>my </i>attention and helps the Scion to progress or helps the storyline to evolve, I'll grant XP through PM. You might spend them whenever you feel like you need an extra dot or Boon. It might ease the tasks but we're not playing to frustrate the players <i>all the time</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don't think I'll be changing the way I'll grant XP. If you disagree with how to spend them, however, we may proceed differently (as the book suggests).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T14:45:03-08:00","id":87015,"title":"","content":"I've seen systems like this work very well, and I've seen them work terribly. It all depends on the players and ST. The only way to know for sure is to try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T15:30:02-08:00","id":87040,"title":"","content":"Oh I forgot to mention how far I want the game to go...<br /> I always plan 'til God-level. Never get to there (only twice 'til demigod-level). Demigod powers are much more interesting for players so I'd like to reach the demigod level. Though, I'm pretty impatient about Scion Origin, so... we'll see how far we will be when the book will be released. Is that okay with you all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T15:53:31-08:00","id":87049,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Am I to understand then that you plan to convert the game when enough of 2E is out for us to do so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:07:07-08:00","id":87057,"title":"","content":"I might, depending on the new system. Of course, everyone will have to agree with first","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:45:36-08:00","id":87076,"title":"","content":"Fine by me, I have a home game I'm, planning that's essentially waiting for the 2E stuff to come out. I expect to do a whole bunch of conversions at home, so may as well do them here too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:47:29-08:00","id":87079,"title":"","content":"XP and posting systems both sound good to me -- and I'm A-Okay with advancing to God level, especially since I may or may not have a secret agenda re: adding &quot;god of hugs&quot; to my Scions eventual titles.<br /> <br /> JK JK .. . maybe.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have a good place to upload character sheets for Scion? Should I just use google docs or something?<br /> <br /> ETA: For one of my characters birthrights, I'm considering using something to do with Vasuki's venom, which has been held in Shiva's throat for eons. Should I PM you about that, Wickedgrail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","user":"Murder-chan","date":". 03-08-2014, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:51:24-08:00","id":87080,"title":"","content":"Upload them? I was just planning to post mine as a message in the eventual OOC thread, once we get going, and once the final draft of the sheet is approved by Fearless Leader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:53:29-08:00","id":87082,"title":"","content":"Oh, here's a question- how do you want to handle dice rolls? Do you just want to roll for all of us and tell us the results, or is there a particular site you want us using?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T18:35:44-08:00","id":87133,"title":"","content":"Does this forum have a chatroom like Rpgpost.com, or maybe there might be an online dice-roller we could all use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T19:43:17-08:00","id":87163,"title":"","content":"Assuming that Grail wants us to roll our own dice, there are any number of dice rolling websites out there. I suggest this one. It is easy to use and to verify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T08:48:52-07:00","id":87509,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I've worked until this afternoon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/82799-looking-for-players-for-scion?p=87079#post87079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ETA: For one of my characters birthrights, I'm considering using something to do with Vasuki's venom, which has been held in Shiva's throat for eons. Should I PM you about that, Wickedgrail?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, PM me, please.<br /> <br /> For character sheet, not everyone needs to see it since you all play your own character. I would have suggested to update the character sheet PM but I don't think it's possible. Anyway, PM will be enough. Just post a new PM every time you need to tell you what's changed.<br /> <br /> As for the dice rolls, I really wasn't planning to ask you to do any. I don't think playing it like a pen and paper rpg will be entertaining. However, I can't find another way. Just hope that battles won't last too long...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:01:58-07:00","id":87579,"title":"","content":"No dice rolls? Then what is the point of character sheets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:21:25-07:00","id":87605,"title":"","content":"That's what I said: Since I can't find another way than rolling dice, we will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/co